, the 8 world pins, and\u001b[48GManifest's on its next\u001b[71Gpin bump.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mThe contract\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mHooks:\u001b[12G\u001b[22m\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mSimWorld::RegisterSystem(desc, Sim::Quiet)\u001b[39m,\u001b[56Gwhich\u001b[62Gkeeps\u001b[68G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mEcs::SystemDescription\u001b[91G\u001b[39mgeneric.\u001b[100G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mQuiet\u001b[106G\u001b[39mhas\u001b[110Gtwo\u001b[114Ghooks:\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5G- \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mnext(const SimWorld&) → step\u001b[39m: the first step at which th\u001b[64G system must really run, giv\u001b[94G the state and no commands\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B \u001b[7Gqueued. It must have no side eff\u001b[40Gcts, and an\u001b[52Gearlier answer is always\u001b[77Gsafe.\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B-\u001b[7G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mskip(SimWorld&, double lastBegan)\u001b[39m: leave\u001b[76Gping the\u001b[85Ggap\u001b[89Gwould\u001b[95Ghave\u001b[100Gleft.\u001b[106GThe\u001b[110Gclock\u001b[116Ghas\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
