[0.118, "o", "\u001b[H\r\u001b[4C\u001b[13B   \u001b[9G  \u001b[12G   \u001b[16G \u001b[18G     \u001b[24G \u001b[26G         \u001b[36G    \u001b[41G   \u001b[45G     \u001b[51G    \u001b[56G   \u001b[60G     \u001b[66G    \u001b[71G    \u001b[76G     \u001b[82G       \u001b[90G     \u001b[96G   \u001b[100G         \u001b[110G     \r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mA flown entity on rails without a body isn't something I expect.\u001b[22m A ship with \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mFlightControls\u001b[39m and \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mHandling\u001b[39m is\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bn\u001b[7Grmally either:\u001b[22G\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B-\u001b[7Ga\u001b[9Gdynamic\u001b[17Gbody\u001b[22Gin\u001b[25Gflight,\u001b[33Gwhere\u001b[39Gphysics\u001b[47Gisn't\u001b[53Gquiet\u001b[59Ganyway;\u001b[67Gor\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B- a kinematic body docked on a station's rails in that station's\u001b[70Gframe,\u001b[78Ghich the flight check leaves to\u001b[110Gphysics.\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1BNeither the\u001b[17Gsample nor Manifest build\u001b[43G the kind\u001b[53Gof \u001b[57Gntit\u001b[62G F6 used.\u001b[72GThe\u001b[76Greviewer\u001b[85Gconstructed\u001b[97Git\u001b[100Gto\u001b[103Gprobe\u001b[109Gthe\u001b[113Gpublic\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bcontract, be\u001b[18Gause nothing\u001b[31Gi\u001b[34Gthe API forbids it. The same goes for F4's\u001b[77Gbody-less\u001b[87Gsh\u001b[90Gp holding\u001b[100Gto a reference,\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Band\u001b[9GF3's\u001b[14Gkinematic\u001b[24Gship\u001b[29Goutside\u001b[37Gany\u001b[41Gframe.\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mI still fixed them\u001b[22m because the promise is bit identity for any\u001b[68Gw\u001b[71Gld, not only today's\u001b[92Ggames. Each fix is\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bconservative: such\u001b[24Gan enti\u001b[32Gy just runs every\u001b[50Gstep\u001b[55Ginstead\u001b[63Gof\u001b[66Gbeing\u001b[72Gpassed\u001b[79Gover.\u001b[85GThey\u001b[90Gcost\u001b[95GManifest\u001b[104Gnothing\u001b[27;1H"]
