[0.004, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[9G\u001b[2m3\u001b[12G\u001b[22m \u001b[14Gswept on from where it was put. The skip also\u001b[60Gplaces every entity on\u001b[83Grails and each local\u001b[104Gframe's\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 554 \u001b[22m   origin and velocity over the last step.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 555 \u001b[22m - **Flight** has to run while a ship's velocity would change, or while one is flown against a\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 556 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  reference with a velocity, which may change step to step; a kinematic body's in a frame it changes  \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m 557 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  only for physics to write over. `Thrust` is not state, and is left as the last step wrote it.       \r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m556\u001b[12G\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m \u001b[14Greferenc\u001b[23G with\u001b[29Ga ve\u001b[34Gocity or\u001b[43Gis on\u001b[49Grails,\u001b[56Geither\u001b[63Gof\u001b[66Gwhich\u001b[72Gmay\u001b[76Gchange\u001b[83Gwhat\u001b[88Git\u001b[91Gis\u001b[94Gheld\u001b[99Gto\u001b[102Gstep\u001b[107Gto\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 557 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  \u001b[48;2;4;71;0mstep; a kinematic body's in a frame it changes \u001b[48;2;2;40;0monly for physics to write over. `Thrust` is not state\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m, and is left as the last step wrote it.                                                              \r\u001b[7C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[2m58\u001b[12G\u001b[22m-\u001b[14G**Cruise** runs in\u001b[33Gthe step that places\u001b[54Gan arrival, and its skip places \u001b[87Gach ship along its\u001b[106Gcour\u001b[111Ge.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 559 \u001b[14G\u001b[22m**Lanes**\u001b[24Grun\u001b[28Gin\u001b[31Gthe\u001b[35Gstep\u001b[40Gan\u001b[43Garrival\u001b[51Gends\u001b[56Gat,\u001b[60G**gates**\u001b[70Gat\u